<h3 id="the-todo-api-architecture" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>The TODO API architecture</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#the-todo-api-architecture" aria-label="Link to The TODO API architecture"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>This is the high-level architecture of the TODO API, where a different Lambda function handles each CRUD operation.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img src="https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/ephemeral-environments-aws-serverless/image-7-67b311ee.png" alt="Image"/></span></span></p>
<p>Everything is configured with the <a href="https://serverless.com/">Serverless Framework</a> and deployed as a single unit.</p>
<p>As shown below, each function has its own handler module. Shared code between the functions is kept in the same project folder.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img src="https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/ephemeral-environments-aws-serverless/image-8-663357c7.png" alt="Image"/></span></span></p>
